.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt SYNC 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sync
.Nd commit accepted file-server changes and flush the device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Wait for the file server to commit all changes it has already accepted,
from every session, and flush the backing device.
This is a durability barrier for accepted work.
It does not order writes still in flight in another process; arrange that
process's completion before requesting the barrier.
A successful call neither reserves space nor establishes a snapshot against
later writers.
.Pp
Normally no text is printed.
.Fl v
prints
.Ql commit Ar sequence
on standard output, identifying the committed device sequence.
No other argument forms are accepted, including
.Ql --
or repeated flags.
.Pp
The file server also commits on written-file close, session end, and at
most about 200 ms after an unsynced write.
This command requires an active file-server channel, not a block handle.
An absent channel, one lent to a running child, refusal or commit failure
is diagnosed on standard error.
It grants no access to otherwise invisible files.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after a successful barrier; 1 for file-server failure; 2 for usage.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo saved > /home/operator/note
sync -v
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cp 1 ,
.Xr df 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr handles 7
